{%- import "lib.j2" as lib -%}
{#-
  Span starters (ADR D2), one class per tier: Qyl.Spans for stable span groups (plus the
  application scope's Source and Work), Qyl.IncubatingSpans for the rest. A group gets
  a starter only when registry/qyl/policy.yaml marks it `starter: true`, which it does only for
  groups no library qyl subscribes to already emits.

  Parameters follow the requirement level mechanically: Required is positional, ConditionallyRequired
  is nullable with no default (omitting one is CS7036, so the caller writes `null` on purpose),
  Recommended defaults to null, and OptIn, `qyl.phase: end`, template and deprecated attributes,
  and the attributes the group fixes, get no parameter. Within each level the root's system
  discriminator comes first, then the keys in ordinal order; a consumer span takes its producer's
  context right after the conditional parameters. Every supplied value is a creation tag, so
  samplers see it, and the group's qyl.instrumentation.domain is stamped.
-#}
